Ticket 001 — Windows 11 Low Disk Space

Category: Windows OS / Storage Management
Environment: Personal Windows 11 laptop
Ticket Type: Self-directed troubleshooting exercise
Status: Resolved

1. Problem Description

The Windows 11 computer had limited available storage, reducing the capacity available for additional software and virtual machines.

The objective was to identify the primary sources of disk usage, safely remove unnecessary files and applications, and verify that sufficient storage had been recovered.

2. Troubleshooting Process

Reviewed available disk space on the Windows 11 system.

Investigated files and installed applications consuming storage.

Identified accumulated files in the Downloads directory as a significant contributor to storage usage.

Reviewed unnecessary applications, including software no longer required.

Uninstalled selected applications and cleaned up unnecessary downloaded files.

Rechecked disk usage to evaluate the results.

3. Root Cause

Excessive storage consumption was primarily associated with accumulated downloaded files, with unused applications also contributing to disk usage.

4. Resolution

Removed unnecessary downloaded files and applications to recover available storage capacity.

5. Verification

Subsequent storage checks showed increased available disk space, ultimately reaching approximately 54.5 GB free.

The original low-storage condition was improved through cleanup. No hardware replacement or operating system reinstallation was required.

6. Lessons Learned

Check storage usage before assuming that disk capacity must be upgraded.

Investigate folders containing large or accumulated files.

Use built-in Windows utilities to diagnose storage issues.

Verify a corrective action by comparing system measurements.

Document troubleshooting steps for future reference.

7. Evidence

Attach available screenshots of Windows storage information and relevant cleanup results, with personal information removed.

8. Outcome

Resolved: Identified significant sources of storage consumption, performed cleanup, and verified recovered disk space.
